# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out
# with CRLF endings. A bash script with CRLF does not merely warn -- every
# line ends in a stray \r, so "read -r model" becomes an invalid identifier
# and the script collapses. Force LF everywhere; nothing in this repository
# is consumed by a tool that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
